@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# GATR2 pipeline
+
+The robot has to know where it is and where things around it are, so it can
+line up with them. The Pico reads the sensors. The Pi turns the readings into a
+robot pose and field-object estimates. The Brain asks the Pi for them, plans
+and drives. The viewer watches the Pi and never commands anything.
+
+```text
+encoders, IMU -> Pico --+
+                        +--> Pi <-- Brain link --> Brain -> motors
+camera -----------------+    |
+                             +--> viewer
+```
+
+| Step | Folder | In | Out |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1. Acquisition | [pico/aggreGATR/](pico/aggreGATR/README.md) | encoders, IMU | sensor frames |
+| 2. Estimation | [pi/naviGATR/](pi/naviGATR/PIPELINE.md) | sensor frames, camera, Brain requests | robot pose, field estimates |
+| 3. Brain link | [translaGATR/](translaGATR/), [brain/communiGATR/](brain/communiGATR/README.md) | requests, replies | state and field on the Brain |
+| 4. Planning and driving | [brain/investiGATR/](brain/investiGATR/README.md), [brain/actuGATR/](brain/actuGATR/README.md) | state, field, destination | motor commands |
+| 5. Viewer | [pi/naviGATR/spectaGATR/](pi/naviGATR/spectaGATR/) | inspection feed, capture ZIPs | nothing to the robot |
+
+## 1. Acquisition: Pico
+
+[pico/aggreGATR/](pico/aggreGATR/README.md), RP2040 on the Pi HAT.
+
+- In: three quadrature encoders; IMU yaw rate over SPI (BNO08X or ASM330LHHG1,
+  picked at build time).
+- Out: timestamped sensor frames to the Pi over UART at 50 Hz; status frames
+  every 200 ms; diagnostic frames only when the Pi asks.
+- Takes Pi commands on the same UART: IMU enable, IMU reinit, acquisition
+  restart, diagnostic rate.
+- No estimation here.
+
+## 2. Estimation: Pi
+
+[pi/naviGATR/](pi/naviGATR/PIPELINE.md), one C++ program.
+
+- In: Pico sensor frames, camera frames, Brain requests (robot profile,
+  placement, control).
+- Out: robot pose (odometry, field anchor, velocity, health), field-object
+  estimates (nominal pose plus error), field documents, the inspection feed.
+- Stages: resources -> sensors -> commands -> localization -> world estimation
+  -> targets -> publishing.
+
+## 3. Brain link
+
+Wire contract: [translaGATR/](translaGATR/) (frames, codec, documents; shared
+by Pico, Pi and Brain), spec in [docs/interfaces.md](docs/interfaces.md). Brain
+side: [brain/communiGATR/](brain/communiGATR/README.md).
+
+- Brain asks, Pi answers each request at most once, never unasked. RS-485 half
+  duplex or the V5 USB console.
+- Brain to Pi: HELLO, PROFILE_WRITE and PROFILE_APPLY (the robot description),
+  SET_POSE, GET_STATE (every 20 ms), READ_DOC, CONTROL, PATH_REPORT,
+  READ_WHEELS.
+- Pi to Brain: the state block (pose, age, health, profile status, document
+  ids), the field map and field estimate documents in chunks.
+
+## 4. Planning and driving: Brain
+
+[brain/investiGATR/](brain/investiGATR/README.md) plans,
+[brain/actuGATR/](brain/actuGATR/README.md) drives,
+[brain/robot/](brain/robot/README.md) describes the robot. Programs:
+[brain/locaGATR/](brain/locaGATR/README.md) (bench, no motors),
+[brain/operaGATR/](brain/operaGATR/README.md) (driving).
+
+- In: robot state and field from communiGATR (`investigatr::StateSource`).
+- Out: motor commands. A destination resolves against the field origin, a map
+  object or the robot pose at command start; the path goes direct or around
+  the field's collision boxes; it is followed from pose feedback on tank or
+  mecanum drives.
+- The Brain owns destinations, offsets from landmarks, mechanisms and motors.
+
+## 5. Viewer
+
+[pi/naviGATR/spectaGATR/](pi/naviGATR/spectaGATR/), served by the Pi's
+inspection service
+([pi/naviGATR/src/debug/inspection/](pi/naviGATR/src/debug/inspection/)).
+
+- In: the `navigatr.inspect/2` feed over loopback HTTP/WebSocket (SSH port
+  forward), capture ZIPs for replay.
+- Out: nothing to the robot.
+- Docs: [inspection](pi/naviGATR/docs/inspection.md),
+  [capture](pi/naviGATR/docs/capture.md).
+
+Boards: [pcb/](pcb/README.md). Names: [docs/naming.md](docs/naming.md).
