+# core
+
+The engine: builds the pipeline once, then runs it. Nothing else.
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| [system.h](system.h) | `System`: build, start, stop, reset, step, snapshot readers |
+| [build.cpp](build.cpp) | `System::build`: parse the XML, call each stage's `make_*` in run order |
+| [run.cpp](run.cpp) | the cycles, the two workers, `step()`, reset, snapshots |
+| [handoff.h](handoff.h) | `LatestSlot`: latest-wins handoff to the field worker; worker counters |
+
+## Build: once, before anything runs
+
+```text
+main: registerAll(functions)         pipeline/register_all.cpp
+System::buildFromFile                config/composition: resolve file references
+System::build
+  <Loop> <Inspection> <Capture>
+  make_resources                     pipeline/resources/stage
+  make_sensors                       pipeline/sensors/stage
+  <CommandCollection type>           slot factory
+  make_localization                  pipeline/localization/stage (waiting noop with <BrainProfile>)
+  make_world_estimation              pipeline/world_estimation/stage
+  <TargetResolution type>            slot factory
+  <Publishing type>                  slot factory
+  capture recorder
+```
+
+- Any error returns no system; nothing partial runs.
+- Factories copy what they need from the XML; node views die after build.
+- Every slot is required. An unused one selects its `noop`.
+
+## Run: every cycle
+
+```text
+estimationCycle   resources -> sensors -> commands -> localization
+                  (+ Brain profile watch, recovery, Pico operation)
+fieldCycle        world estimation on a SensorMap copy -> FieldSnapshot
+reportingCycle    targets -> publishing, against the newest FieldSnapshot
+```
+
+- Workers (`start`/`stop`): the estimation worker runs `estimationCycle`, puts
+  the SensorMap into the `LatestSlot`, then `reportingCycle`, at
+  `<Loop rate_hz>`. The field worker runs `fieldCycle` on whatever is newest.
+- Inline (`step`): profile swap, `estimationCycle`, `fieldCycle`,
+  `reportingCycle`, on the caller's thread. Tests and replay.
+- `reset()` stops both workers, resets every stage once, restarts them.
+- Brain profile swaps and recovery live in
+  [src/brain_profile/](../brain_profile/), called from here at controlled
+  boundaries.
