@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# targets
+
+Turns a selected target into a desired robot pose. One slot,
+`<TargetResolution type>`.
+
+- In: command, robot state, pose history, committed field, published
+  observations and associations, previous target.
+- Out: `TargetState` ([target_state.h](target_state.h)): the active target,
+  latched in the odometry frame.
+- Contract: [contract.h](contract.h) `TargetResolution`,
+  `TargetResolutionMakeFunction`.
+- No stage builder: [core/build.cpp](../../core/build.cpp) builds the slot.
+- Landmark-relative targets move with the landmark through
+  `applyLandmarkError` ([field_state.h](../world_estimation/field_state.h)).
+- Pi internal: inspection shows targets, the Brain link never sends them.
+
+Plug-ins: `resolvers/` (`configured_targets`, `noop`), registered in
+[resolvers/register_target_resolution.cpp](resolvers/register_target_resolution.cpp).
+Targets themselves are XML data (`target_set` resource).
+
+Add one: a `TargetResolution` implementation in `resolvers/`, a line in
+`register_target_resolution.cpp`, the source in CMake.
