+# world_estimation
+
+Where are things around me, well enough to line up with them. The goal is to
+be somewhere relative to a field object, not to know exactly where that object
+is on the field.
+
+## Contract
+
+- In ([contract.h](contract.h) `FieldEstimationInput`): the whole `SensorMap`,
+  the latest `RobotState`, pose history lookups, the previous `FieldState`, the
+  execution context.
+- Out (`FieldEstimationOutput`): `FieldState`, the published `ObservationMap`
+  and `AssociationMap`, status, diagnostic.
+- Runs on the field worker, on the newest SensorMap, whether or not a target is
+  requested. Seeing a displaced goal moves the goal's estimate, never the
+  robot.
+- Builder: [stage.h](stage.h) `make_world_estimation`.
+
+## One estimator
+
+```xml
+<WorldEstimation>
+    <Estimator id="goals" type="apriltag">...</Estimator>
+</WorldEstimation>
+```
+
+- Exactly one `<Estimator>`. The stage refuses zero or more than one.
+- An estimator is a sensor group: its sensors, its own config, and the steps
+  that turn them into full-pose evidence of field objects. Partial
+  measurements, time alignment and association stay inside the group.
+- Today: `apriltag`, and `noop` (previous field carried forward, nothing
+  published).
+- No fusion step. Evidence is pose only; a range/bearing form waits for a real
+  second sensor.
+
+## Output: LandmarkError
+
+Each mapped object in `FieldState` ([field_state.h](field_state.h)) carries:
+
+- `pose`: the estimated field pose;
+- `nominal`: where the map says it is;
+- `error`: `LandmarkError{dx, dy, dtheta}`, pose minus nominal in field axes,
+  `dtheta` wrapped.
+
+(0, 0, 0) is the field as built. The map's heading zero is an authoring
+convention and means nothing. `pose` = nominal + error: position = nominal +
+(dx, dy), heading = wrap(nominal heading + dtheta).
+
+- An observed pose is kept in the odometry frame it was measured in
+  (`T_odom_object`, odometry epoch). The field pose and the error are derived
+  under the current anchor; a new odometry epoch drops it back to nominal.
+- `applyLandmarkError(error, landmark_nominal, target_nominal)` moves a target
+  defined relative to a landmark: its offset from the nominal landmark rotates
+  by dtheta, then shifts by (dx, dy); heading + dtheta. Target resolution uses
+  it.
+- Inspection's `heading_error_deg` and `displacement_m` read the error.
+- The Brain wire still sends full poses (nominal plus error).
+
+## Error budget
+
+- Localization error at the sighting is in both the landmark error (dx, dy) and
+  the robot pose, so it cancels for a target defined relative to that landmark.
+- What is left, main: perception error (tag detection, camera calibration,
+  mount geometry).
+- What is left, second: localization drift since the last sighting. It does not
+  cancel. Landmark-anchored targets re-resolve every cycle while the tag stays
+  in view, which keeps it small.
+
+## Layout
+
+Generic, any sensor group:
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| [contract.h](contract.h) | stage in/out |
+| [stage.h](stage.h), [stage.cpp](stage.cpp) | `make_world_estimation`, the executor, the one-estimator rule |
+| [perception.h](perception.h), [association.h](association.h) | step contracts an estimator may use inside |
+| [evidence.h](evidence.h) | `FieldObjectPoseEvidence(Set)`: an object pose with frame, measurement time, odometry epoch |
+| [field_state.h](field_state.h) | `FieldState`, `LandmarkError`, `applyLandmarkError` |
+| [landmark_estimator.h](landmark_estimator.h) | folds evidence into `FieldState`; never knows the sensor |
+
+Sensor groups, [estimators/](estimators/register_world_estimation.cpp):
+
+| Folder | What |
+|---|---|
+| [estimators/apriltag/](estimators/apriltag/PIPELINE.md) | tag extraction, tag mount association, tag observation payloads, `TagAssociationTrace`, `AprilTagWorldEstimator` |
+| `estimators/noop/` | previous field forward, nothing published |
+
+Inside `apriltag`:
+
+```text
+SensorMap -> ObservationExtraction -> tag observations
+          -> Association (tag mounts, pose at exposure) -> FieldObjectPoseEvidenceSet
+          -> LandmarkEstimation -> FieldState
+```
+
+Add a sensor group: `estimators/<group>/` with a `FieldEstimation`
+implementation that turns its sensors into `FieldObjectPoseEvidence` and folds
+it with `LandmarkEstimator`; a line in
+[register_world_estimation.cpp](estimators/register_world_estimation.cpp); the
+source in CMake; select it by `type`. Details:
+[docs/landmarks.md](../../../docs/landmarks.md).
